-- title:
--   Hasse root function outside κ(X₁(M))_q in characteristic three
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $M$ with $M \neq 0$, $5 \le M$ and $3 \nmid M$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $3$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$, that is: a modular form `form` of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ (taken as a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), a power series `series` over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the width-one $q$-expansion of `form`, together with the requirement that the reduction `intSeriesC κ w.series` — the image of `series` under $\mathbb{Z} \to \kappa$, regarded as a Laurent series in $\kappa((q))$ — be nonzero. The element in question, `w.hasseRootFn`, is the inverse in $\kappa((q))$ of that reduced $q$-expansion. The assertion is that this inverse does not lie in [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC κ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134), the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC κ (Gamma1 M)`, the $q$-expansion model of the function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\kappa$. Since that intermediate field is a field and the reduced series is nonzero, this is equivalent to the reduced $q$-expansion of $w$ itself not lying in it.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$3$ instance of the statement that the Igusa covering of $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$ is of degree $p-1$ rather than split: the reciprocal of the reduced weight-one $q$-expansion, a $(p-1)$st root of the Hasse invariant, generates a nontrivial extension of the level-$M$ $q$-expansion function field. It is used in computing the degree of $X_1(M)$ inside the Igusa function field and in the construction of the associated Igusa diamond data at $p=3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_hasseRootFn_notMem_x1FunctionFieldC_charThree.lean

